<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Razor">

	<PropertyGroup>
		<TargetFramework>net10.0</TargetFramework>
		<!-- Deploy wwwroot contents to the app's root, not _content/SpawnDev.WebTorrent/ -->
		<!-- Required for service worker scope — SW must be at app root to intercept all requests -->
		<StaticWebAssetBasePath Condition="$(StaticWebAssetBasePath) == ''">/</StaticWebAssetBasePath>
		<LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
		<ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
		<Nullable>enable</Nullable>
		<AllowUnsafeBlocks>true</AllowUnsafeBlocks>
		<Version>3.1.3-rc.18</Version>
		<PackageReleaseNotes>v3.1.3-rc.18: `WebTorrentClient.Add` now wires the ut_metadata extension factory into v2 mode automatically when the magnet is pure-v2 (urn:btmh: only, no urn:btih:). The extension advertises `metadata_version: 2` in its BEP 10 extended handshake, and OnMetadata parses via `TorrentParser.ParseInfoDictV2` (SHA-256-verified against the full v2 hash). Hybrid + v1-only stay on the v1 path unchanged. Plus new `TorrentParser.ParseInfoDictV2(bytes, expectedV2InfoHash)` helper. 2 new tests cover the factory wiring end-to-end on both pure-v2 and v1-only magnets. v3.1.3-rc.17: Multi-tracker failover resilience. `Discovery.AnnounceAsync` now isolates per-tracker failures — one unreachable WSS host, HTTP 5xx, or UDP timeout no longer cancels the aggregate `Task.WhenAll` that dispatches announces to the other trackers. Errors surface via `OnWarning` with the failing tracker URL + exception type; downstream loops keep running. 2 new tests in `TrackerFailoverTests` cover the "one bad tracker among good ones" case and the "all trackers down" case (client stays alive, torrent registered, no cascade). Closes Gap 6 of Geordi's P2P audit on the WebTorrent side. v3.1.3-rc.16: `TorrentCreator.CreateFromMultipleStreamsAsync` now supports Hybrid=true. Single-pass streaming: each read feeds both the v2 IncrementalMerkleHasher AND the v1 piece-buffered SHA-1 hasher. Known-up-front declared lengths let us compute pad-file alignment without a second scan. End-of-file emits a full zero-padded v1 piece for non-last files (matching the pad-file-filled virtual stream) and a genuine partial piece for the last file. Output byte-identical to the in-memory `BuildHybridMultiFile` path; info dict + both info hashes + file tree + piece layers match exactly. Lifts the rc.13 restriction on hybrid streaming. v3.1.3-rc.15: Diagnostic build for Geordi's rc.12 two-popup mystery. Field test showed the channel-Label tiebreaker firing correctly BUT against an "existing" wire whose SimplePeer.ChannelName is empty — which per code invariants should not be possible (Wire.PeerId only gets set in _onHandshakeBuffer which runs after OnDataChannel has set ChannelName). rc.15 adds two diagnostic logs to pinpoint the phantom: (1) RtcPeer.OnDataChannel responder path logs the exact ChannelName set after assignment; (2) Torrent.OnHandshake duplicate branch dumps the full Wires state (all PeerIds + matching _peers entries + ChannelNames) before the tiebreaker decision. With both logs Geordi can identify whether the phantom is a wire with no _peers entry (destroy-race), a wire whose Conn is not a SimplePeer, or something else. No behavior change — pure diagnostics. v3.1.3-rc.14: ut_metadata v2 variant with metadata_version:2 extended-handshake key + SHA-256 verification. v3.1.3-rc.13: Pure-v2 torrent tracker + wire-handshake support; streaming multi-file creator. v3.1.3-rc.12: Duplicate-peer tiebreaker on WebRTC channel Label. v3.1.3-rc.11: RtcPeer deferred EmitConnect when channel already open. v3.1.3-rc.4: RtcPeer.PeerConnection public getter. v3.1.3-rc.3: SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.3-rc.2 dep bump. v3.1.3-rc.2: Pure-v2 multi-file past file 0. v3.1.3-rc.1: SpawnDev.RTC 1.1.3-rc.1 dep bump.</PackageReleaseNotes>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<EmbedAllSources>true</EmbedAllSources>
		<DebugType>Embedded</DebugType>
		<NoWarn>$(NoWarn);CS1591</NoWarn>
		<Title>SpawnDev.WebTorrent</Title>
		<Authors>LostBeard</Authors>
		<Description>Pure C# BitTorrent/WebTorrent client. 15 BEPs, real WebRTC P2P (browser + desktop), DHT with mutable items (BEP 46 — AI agent communication), web seeds, media streaming with seeking via service worker, OPFS storage. Includes webtorrent-sw.js for COI headers + torrent streaming. No JavaScript dependencies. Runs on desktop (.NET + SIPSorcery) and browser (Blazor WASM + SpawnDev.BlazorJS). 444 unit tests.</Description>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent</PackageProjectUrl>
		<PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
		<PackageLicenseFile>LICENSE.txt</PackageLicenseFile>
		<PackageIcon>icon-128.png</PackageIcon>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.WebTorrent.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
		<PackageTags>BitTorrent;WebTorrent;P2P;Torrent;Blazor;WebAssembly;WebRTC;DHT;Streaming;MachineLearning;ModelDelivery;SIPSorcery</PackageTags>
		<NoPackageAnalysis>true</NoPackageAnalysis>
		<IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
	</PropertyGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Tests" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Demo.Shared" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="Assets\icon-128.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\LICENSE.txt" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS" Version="3.5.3" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.AsyncFileSystem" Version="1.2.0" />
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.BlazorJS.Cryptography" Version="3.2.0" />
		<!-- SpawnDev.RTC replaces direct SipSorcery dependency - provides cross-platform WebRTC
		     with proven browser-interop SipSorcery fork (SRTP profile fix) bundled inside.
		     PackageReference (not ProjectReference) so CI / GitHub Pages builds work from a
		     standalone SpawnDev.WebTorrent checkout - they don't have the sibling RTC repo.
		     1.1.1 is the minimum version: 1.1.0 declared a dep on public SIPSorcery 10.0.4-pre
		     which doesn't exist on nuget.org; 1.1.1 bundles the fork DLLs inline (ILGPU pattern). -->
		<PackageReference Include="SpawnDev.RTC" Version="1.1.3-rc.3" />
	</ItemGroup>

	<ItemGroup>
		<SupportedPlatform Include="browser" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="windows" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="linux" />
		<SupportedPlatform Include="macos" />
	</ItemGroup>

</Project>
